        {
          "field": "summary",
          "value": "Knightmare, known in Japan as Majou Densetsu (魔城伝説 , Demon Castle Legend?), is a 1986 MSX vertical scrolling shooter computer game. The player is a knight, Popolon, who has to fight his way through several levels to defeat Hudnos and rescue Aphrodite.\n\nKnightmare was an innovative upward-scrolling shoot 'em up game on the MSX system released as game cartridge. The top-view graphics were considered very sophisticated for its time, similar to other MSX games such as Nemesis and Penguin Adventure.\n\nKonami also released a slightly altered version that could be bought from LINKS network. (Japanese \"internet replacement\" of the 80's) In this version you could submit high scores to online server.\n\nIt was brought without a license to the SG-1000 in Taiwan.",
          "source": "igdb",
          "manual": false
        },
        {
